  <section class="page-heading compact-heading section-pad"><div class="page-kicker"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT THIS PREVIEW</span><span>UPDATED SEPTEMBER 2026</span></div><h1>A little<br><em>transparency.</em></h1></section><section class="privacy-content section-pad"><article><h2>The enquiry form</h2><p>The current form is a demonstration. Information you enter is used in your browser to show an enquiry summary and, if you choose, create a text file for you to download. The form does not upload your entries, send an email or WhatsApp message, or save a client record.</p><p>Refreshing or leaving the page clears the form’s in-page state. Your browser may offer its own autofill features. If you download a brief, that file is saved on your device.</p></article><article><h2>Demo contact details</h2><p>The email address and phone number shown on the contact page are placeholders. They are not active contact channels. Real contact details and the final enquiry handling process will need to be added before the form is used for client enquiries.</p></article><article><h2>Reference projects & drawings</h2><p>The project photographs, locations, sizes and descriptions form an illustrative portfolio concept. They are not a verified record of completed Archcell commissions. Photography credits are available in the footer.</p><p>All drawing sheets are sample diagrams, not to scale and not for construction. They must not be used for site works, engineering decisions or installation.</p></article><article><h2>Website services</h2><p>The site is hosted through Sites. Its hosting provider may process routine connection information when serving the website. The site also requests typefaces from Google Fonts, which receives the connection information needed to deliver those font files.</p><p>Archcell has not added advertising trackers or analytics scripts to this preview.</p></article><article><h2>When the site goes live for enquiries</h2><p>This page will need to be updated with the studio’s real contact information, the service receiving enquiries, how enquiries are used and retained, and how visitors can raise a privacy question.</p></article><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Return to the enquiry page <span>↗</span></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
